        "comments": "The assembly fPimPro1.hap1.1 is based on 126x Oxford Nanopore data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial Oxford Nanopore assembly generation with Hifiasm in Hi-C integrated assembly mode, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, each haplotype assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 2 (27,265 ? 29,192 & 49,860 ? 53,071 Kbp) are unknown. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 3 (44,664 ? 47,320 Kbp) are unknown. A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 5 (13,808 - 19,004 Kbp). A haplotypic inversion was observed in the region on chromosome 9 (19,821 ? 22,594 Kbp).",
